@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki"

Feature: Koroneiki Team API
	Testing Koroneiki Team API functionality.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the teams on koroneiki with the following names
	| Development Team |
	| Marketing Team   |
	| Engineering Team |
	| Sales Team       |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Auto Subsidiary |
	| Koroneiki Engr Subsidiary |
	| Koroneiki Automotive      |
	| Koroneiki Engineering     |

Scenario: Create and view team
	Koroneiki teams created via API should be viewable via API.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                                  | |
	| Contact Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki     | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                             | |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                     | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                             | |
	| Profile Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                            | |
	| Status                | Active                                   | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                       | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | |
	And I create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki team with the name "Development Team"
	And the team with the name "Development Team" should be part of the account "Koroneiki Automotive"

Scenario: Create and view multiple teams
	Multiple teams created via API should be viewable via API.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                                  | |
	| Contact Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki     | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                             | |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                     | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                             | |
	| Profile Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                            | |
	| Status                | Active                                   | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                       | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | |
	And I create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I create a team with the name "Marketing Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki team with the name "Development Team"
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki team with the name "Marketing Team"
	And the team with the name "Development Team" should be part of the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the team with the name "Marketing Team" should be part of the account "Koroneiki Automotive"

Scenario: Create and view multiple teams on separate accounts
	Multiple teams created via API for separate accounts should be viewable via API.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                                  | |
	| Contact Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki     | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                             | |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                     | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                             | |
	| Profile Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                            | |
	| Status                | Active                                   | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                       | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORENGR                                  | |
	| Contact Email Address | koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test engineering account on koroneiki    | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-4321                             | |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Engineering                    | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-8765                             | |
	| Profile Email Address | koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | Japan                                    | |
	| Status                | Active                                   | |
	| Tier                  | T1                                       | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiengineering.com             | |
	And I create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I create a team with the name "Marketing Team" for the account "Koroneiki Engineering"
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki team with the name "Development Team"
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki team with the name "Marketing Team"
	And the team with the name "Development Team" should be part of the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the team with the name "Marketing Team" should be part of the account "Koroneiki Engineering"
	And the team with the name "Development Team" should not be part of the account "Koroneiki Engineering"
	And the team with the name "Marketing Team" should not be part of the account "Koroneiki Automotive"

Scenario: Create and view teams on account and child account
	Multiple teams created via API for separate parent and child accounts should be viewable via API.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                                  | |
	| Contact Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki     | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                             | |
