	| Status                | Active                                   | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                       | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | |
	And I create a child account for an account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTOSUB                                 | |
	| Contact Email Address | koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken   | |
	| Description           | Test automotive child account on koroneiki | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-9012                               | |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Auto Subsidiary                  | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-3456                               | |
	| Profile Email Address | koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken   | |
	| Region                | United States                              | |
	| Status                | Active                                     | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                         | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotivesubsidiary.com      | |
	And I create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I create a team with the name "Marketing Team" for the account "Koroneiki Auto Subsidiary"
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki team with the name "Development Team"
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki team with the name "Marketing Team"
	And the team with the name "Development Team" should be part of the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the team with the name "Marketing Team" should be part of the account "Koroneiki Auto Subsidiary"
	And the team with the name "Development Team" should not be part of the account "Koroneiki Auto Subsidiary"
	And the team with the name "Marketing Team" should not be part of the account "Koroneiki Automotive"

Scenario: Update and view team
	Koroneiki teams updated via API should be viewable via API.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                                  | |
	| Contact Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki     | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                             | |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                     | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                             | |
	| Profile Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                            | |
	| Status                | Active                                   | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                       | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | |
	And I create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I update a team with the name "Development Team" to have the new name "Marketing Team"
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki team with the name "Marketing Team"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki team with the name "Development Team"
	And the team with the name "Marketing Team" should be part of the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the team with the name "Development Team" should not be part of the account "Koroneiki Automotive"

Scenario: Attempt to update default team and view
	Koroneiki default teams should not be able to be updated via API.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                                  | |
	| Contact Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki     | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                             | |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                     | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                             | |
	| Profile Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                            | |
	| Status                | Active                                   | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                       | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | |
	And I attempt to update a team with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" to have the new name "Development Team"
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki team with the name "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki team with the name "Development Team"
	And the team with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" should be part of the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the team with the name "Development Team" should not be part of the account "Koroneiki Automotive"

